{
  "strategic_goal": "Accept the Accelerationist's point that 'hack' is an accusation, not a finding. Then show that the CFAA question cannot be settled until someone other than OpenAI can verify what happened. Move the debate from 'did they or didn't they' to the observable questions: who holds which records, who will check them, and who answers if an agent did the work.",
  "core_thesis": "No one has yet shown that OpenAI broke through a real gate on Hugging Face or any other site, and the public record cannot show it yet. That gap is not proof of innocence. It is a verification problem that the CFAA, as now used, leaves to the accused firm to resolve.",
